# XML editing guardrails

- Keep indentation, tag casing, and ordering consistent with neighboring entries.
- Do not rename IDs, keys, or source references unless all references are updated.
- Prefer additive edits for new content; avoid restructuring existing XML blocks unless required.
- When removing content, ensure dependent collection includes are still valid.

# Validation checklist

After XML edits, verify:

1. The modified file remains well-formed XML.
2. Related collection files still include correct relative paths.
3. The merge/build command runs for at least one affected collection.

# Safe change patterns

- Add new items by copying the closest existing example and editing only required fields.
- When changing shared metadata (e.g., source names), search for all references first.
- Keep text content human-readable; avoid escaping changes unless strictly needed.
